Missing test coverage for error handling when an invalid persistence type is provided in object form. While there's error handling for invalid string persistence types (line 962 in memory-driver.ts), there's no test that validates the behavior for object configs with invalid types like `{ type: 'indexeddb' }`. Add a test to verify that an appropriate error is thrown for this case.
```suggestion
    });

    it('should throw an error for invalid persistence type in object config', async () => {
      const driver = new InMemoryDriver({
        // Cast to any to allow passing an invalid type for testing error handling
        persistence: { type: 'indexeddb' } as any,
      } as any);

      await expect(driver.connect()).rejects.toThrow();
    });
